course: dictionary
lesson: 15857
title: Unfavourable: when the odds are against you
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Unfavourable is an adjective. It means not good or helpful, and it makes success less likely. Look at the words around it to find its meaning: «The weather was unfavourable, so the sports day was moved indoors.» Rain and wind are bad for a sports day, so unfavourable means bad for what you want to do.
explain: The word can also describe an opinion. «The critic wrote an unfavourable review of the film.» Here, unfavourable means the critic did not like the film or approve of it. Ask yourself: is the thing being described working against someone, or does someone dislike it?
explain: Try the swap check. Put a simple meaning into the sentence: «The weather was bad, so the sports day was moved indoors.» It still makes sense, so bad is a good meaning. Unfavourable is a longer, more formal word for the same idea, and it is often used in reports and exams.
fact: Unfavourable means not good or helpful, and it makes success less likely.
fact: «Unfavourable» also means showing that you do not like or approve of something.
fact: The opposite of unfavourable is favourable, which means good, helpful or approving.
fact: In American English the word is spelled unfavorable, without the u.
fact: In games and chance, unfavourable outcomes are the ones you do not want.
exercise: «Conditions were unfavourable for growth, so the seeds did not sprout.» What does unfavourable mean here? | Full of sunshine and water | Quick and easy | Very colourful | *Not good or helpful for growing
exercise: Sam says the review was unfavourable. What does this show? | The reviewer was lost | The reviewer loved the film | The reviewer was very tall | *The reviewer did not like or approve of it
exercise: In a game, which outcome is unfavourable? | *Rolling a 1 when you needed a 5 or 6 to win | Winning the prize | Getting an extra go | Collecting a bonus point
test: «The unfavourable wind blew the kite into a tree.» What does unfavourable mean in this sentence? | Very windy | Silent | *Not good for flying | Helpful for flying
test: Which sentence shows an unfavourable opinion? | «He cheered loudly at the football match.» | «She was delighted with her new bike.» | *«She wrote that the play was dull and too long.»
exam: Which word is the opposite of unfavourable? | Unkind | Heavy | Unlucky | *Favourable
